{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_bdrk_g2dxlf6zq3sctoetneac62n2cmuczpugwfepohhkypputkob7fjq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The translation is complete. Summary of what was implemented in `src/fs.rs`:\n\n- **`fs_error`**: Prints the last OS error to stderr with the given prefix, mimicking `perror`.\n- **`fs_open`**: Parses fopen-style mode strings (`r`, `w`, `a`, with optional `+` and `b`) into `OpenOptions` and returns an `OwnedFd` (or `None` on failure).\n- **`fs_close`**: Drops the `OwnedFd`, closing the underlying descriptor.\n- **`fs_rename`**: Wraps `fs::rename`.\n- **`fs_stat` / `fs_fstat` / `fs_lstat`**: Use `fs::metadata`, `File::metadata` (via a duplicated descriptor), and `fs::symlink_metadata`.\n- **`fs_ftruncate` / `fs_truncate`**: Set the file length using `File::set_len`.\n- **`fs_chown` / `fs_fchown` / `fs_lchown`**: Use `std::os::unix::fs::{chown, fchown, lchown}` on Unix; return `Unsupported` on other platforms.\n- **`fs_size`**: Returns metadata length.\n- **`fs_fsize`**: Mirrors the C version — saves position, seeks to end for size, restores position.\n- **`fs_read` / `fs_nread` / `fs_fread` / `fs_fnread`**: Read full or `n` bytes via a shared `read_n` helper that handles EINTR and short reads.\n- **`fs_write` / `fs_nwrite` / `fs_fwrite` / `fs_fnwrite`**: Write data, with `write_n` capping output to `min(len, data.len())`.\n- **`fs_mkdir`**: Uses `DirBuilderExt::mode` on Unix to honor the mode argument.\n- **`fs_rmdir`**: Wraps `fs::remove_dir`.\n- **`fs_exists`**: Returns `true` if metadata can be retrieved.\n\nA private `fd_to_file` helper duplicates an `&OwnedFd` into a workable `File` so that the FD-based functions can read/write/seek without consuming the caller's descriptor. `cargo build` and `cargo build --release` both succeed cleanly with no warnings."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens